From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] bms: port to android-mainline

One cumulative patch, kept in two sections: the 6.1 -> 6.18 port this
project first needed for GrapheneOS's 6.18 GKI, then 6.18 -> android-mainline.

== 6.1 -> 6.18 ==
(bms: port to Linux 6.18 (lynx))

Port private/google-modules/bms to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
Mechanical API migrations, no intended behaviour change:

  - strlcpy() removed, use strscpy() (6.8)

Files: misc/gvotable.c

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.

== 6.18 -> android-mainline ==

Linux 6.18 -> android-mainline (7.3):

  * of_node_to_fwnode() -> of_fwnode_handle(); irq_domain_add_linear() ->
    irq_domain_create_linear(of_fwnode_handle(np), ...) (as upstream).
  * alarm_start_relative()/alarm_start() -> alarm_start_timer(.., relative).
  * thermal_of_cooling_device_register() gained a cdev_id argument (0, as
    every in-tree caller passes).
  * misc/logbuffer.c: register_syscore_ops() -> register_syscore() with a
    struct syscore; syscore callbacks take a void *data.

lynx-linus-mainline (android-mainline -> Linus' v7.3; ACK-only interfaces are
handled here rather than restored in the kernel, see kernel/patches/README.md):
  * gbms_power_supply.h: POWER_SUPPLY_CHARGE_TYPE_TAPER_EXT (50), an ACK
    addition to enum power_supply_charge_type, defined with the same value.
  * power_supply_get_by_reference_array() (ACK-only) from
    <soc/google/psy-reference-array.h> (soc/gs linus-compat), rebuilt on
    power_supply_for_each_psy() + power_supply_get_by_name().
  * CRC8: GOOGLE_BMS_CRC8 (misc/Kconfig) selects it, so the device build
    makes lib/crc/crc8.ko; Linus' GKI does not build CRC8 in.
  * max1720x_battery, max77779_fg: strncpy() from <soc/google/linus-compat.h>.
  * google_dc_pps: PPS sink-PDO updates need GrapheneOS's
    tcpm_update_sink_capabilities(), which Linus' TCPM lacks; -EOPNOTSUPP,
    charging stays on the device-tree sink PDOs.
  * Kbuild for the ddk_modules here, generated from BUILD.bazel by
    tools/bazel2kbuild.py, for the make-only build (kernel/kbuild.mk):
      Kbuild
